\section{Data}
%====================================================================

\subsection{Corpus and provenance}

The corpus comprises {{N_SOURCES}} primary artifacts: Hugging Face's
interactive intrusion replay \cite{hf_replay}, technical timeline
\cite{hf_timeline} and disclosure \cite{hf_disclosure}; OpenAI's two
statements \cite{openai_disclosure,openai_roadahead} and its
{{OAI_TR_PAGES}}-page technical report \cite{openai_techreport}; and
the {{METR_PAGES}}-page independent investigation by METR and Redwood
Research \cite{metr2026}. Each is retrieved once, stored verbatim, and
recorded in a manifest with its SHA-256 digest, byte length, HTTP
status, retrieval time and an evidential class (\ref{app:prov}). All
later processing reads the cache, so results are reproducible from a
fixed snapshot and an upstream revision surfaces as a digest mismatch
rather than being absorbed.

What the corpus does \emph{not} contain bounds every result below. The
raw {{TOTAL_ACTIONS}}-action log and the approximately 1{,}300 agent
transcripts were reviewed on-premises and never released
\cite{metr2026}; what is public is a \emph{derived} summary of
phase-level aggregates, per-day counts, a cumulative curve and
representative commands. No analysis here requires individual actions,
inter-arrival times or per-agent attribution.

%====================================================================
\section{Methodology}
\label{sec:method}
%====================================================================

\subsection{Extraction and validation}

Ingestion recovers the replay's embedded literals with a scanner that
tracks string state, parses each PDF page-by-page with page locators
retained, parses the technical timeline into sections and captured
command blocks, and assembles a normalised event chronology. Because a
partially-successful parse yields plausible rather than absent output,
each stage asserts a reconciliation condition and halts on failure ---
per-day counts against the cumulative curve and the published total,
page counts and text-recovery rate for each PDF, and every declared
quotation anchor located in the cached bytes. \ref{app:prov} gives the
yields and the two parser failure modes this caught.

\subsection{Phase concurrency and its bound}
\label{sec:conc-method}

Normalise campaign time to $[0,1]$. The replay annotates each phase $p$
with first and last action times, giving an \emph{envelope}
$E_p=[f_p,\ell_p]$ of span $\sigma_p$ and an action count $n_p$. An
envelope is not a duty cycle: a phase with few actions dispersed across
the campaign has a wide envelope while being almost never active. We
therefore define density $\delta_p = n_p/\sigma_p$, restrict inference
to the dense set $D=\{p: n_p \geq \tau\}$ with
$\tau={{DENSE_MIN_ACTIONS}}$ actions, measure overlap
$O(a,b) = |E_a \cap E_b| / \min(\sigma_a,\sigma_b)$, and write
$\Phi_D$ for the measure of $t$ at which every dense phase is within
its envelope.

\paragraph{Why these two statistics are not reported as findings.}
Both are bounded by the spans alone: two intervals in $[0,1]$ intersect
on at least $\max(0,\sigma_a+\sigma_b-1)$, which forces
$O(a,b)$ upward as spans approach 1 and confines $\Phi_D$ between
$1-\sum_{p\in D}(1-\sigma_p)$ and $\min_{p\in D}\sigma_p$. With the
observed spans that leaves $\overline{O}$ in
$[{{OVERLAP_FLOOR}}, 1]$, a band {{OVERLAP_BAND}} wide, and $\Phi_D$ in
$[{{PHI_FLOOR}}\%, {{PHI_CEIL}}\%]$, a band {{PHI_BAND}} percentage
points wide. Once the spans are known neither statistic is free to
report anything but a value close to one: they restate the span column
in two extra symbols. \ref{app:conc} derives the bound and states two
further limits --- the choice of $\tau$, and $\delta_p$ being a mean
rate over an envelope under a markedly non-uniform distribution.

\subsection{Escalation intervals and reproducibility}
\label{sec:intervals}

Events carry a UTC timestamp, an actor, a source, and a distinctive
anchor string. An event is marked \textsc{verified} only if its anchor
is located in the cached bytes of its declared source; events resting
on press reporting are marked \textsc{unverified-secondary} and
retained as the best available account, and any interval computed from
them inherits that status; {{N_EVENTS_VERIFIED}} of
{{N_EVENTS_TOTAL}} events are anchored in a primary source. Every
quantity in this paper is computed from the derived data at build time
and substituted into the manuscript, an unresolvable quantity being a
build failure. That guarantees agreement between manuscript and
artifacts; it does not establish that a measure is appropriate --- see
(L6) in \S\ref{sec:limits}.

